{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-philemon-001",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 1,
  "title": "Philemon 1",
  "display_title": "Philemon 1",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "philemon",
  "book": "Philemon",
  "bookName": "Philemon",
  "bookOrder": 57,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 1,
  "sortOrder": 57001,
  "verseCount": 25,
  "aliases": [
    "Phlm",
    "Phm",
    "Phile"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Paul, a prisoner of Jesus Christ, and Timothy our brother, unto Philemon our dearly beloved, and fellowlabourer,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And to our beloved Apphia, and Archippus our fellowsoldier, and to the church in thy house:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Grace to you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "I thank my God, making mention of thee always in my prayers,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Hearing of thy love and faith, which thou hast toward the Lord Jesus, and toward all saints;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "That the communication of thy faith may become effectual by the acknowledging of every good thing which is in you in Christ Jesus.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For we have great joy and consolation in thy love, because the bowels of the saints are refreshed by thee, brother.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Wherefore, though I might be much bold in Christ to enjoin thee that which is convenient,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Yet for love’s sake I rather beseech thee, being such an one as Paul the aged, and now also a prisoner of Jesus Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "I beseech thee for my son Onesimus, whom I have begotten in my bonds:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Which in time past was to thee unprofitable, but now profitable to thee and to me:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Whom I have sent again: thou therefore receive him, that is, mine own bowels:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Whom I would have retained with me, that in thy stead he might have ministered unto me in the bonds of the gospel:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "But without thy mind would I do nothing; that thy benefit should not be as it were of necessity, but willingly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "For perhaps he therefore departed for a season, that thou shouldest receive him for ever;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Not now as a servant, but above a servant, a brother beloved, specially to me, but how much more unto thee, both in the flesh, and in the Lord?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "If thou count me therefore a partner, receive him as myself.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "If he hath wronged thee, or oweth thee ought, put that on mine account;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "I Paul have written it with mine own hand, I will repay it: albeit I do not say to thee how thou owest unto me even thine own self besides.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Yea, brother, let me have joy of thee in the Lord: refresh my bowels in the Lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Having confidence in thy obedience I wrote unto thee, knowing that thou wilt also do more than I say.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "But withal prepare me also a lodging: for I trust that through your prayers I shall be given unto you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "There salute thee Epaphras, my fellowprisoner in Christ Jesus;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Marcus, Aristarchus, Demas, Lucas, my fellowlabourers.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:philemon:1:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Philemon 1:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:philemon:1:25"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
